From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733-cubie-a7s: Offer DisplayPort pin
 assignment D

The combo PHY can carry two DisplayPort lanes next to USB3. On the
board, lanes 0 and 1 of the PHY go to the SSTX1 and SSRX1 pins of the
connector and lanes 2 and 3 to SSRX2 and SSTX2 (Radxa Cubie A7S
schematic V1.10, sheet 12).

Offer pin assignment D in the DisplayPort mode of the connector, next to
C and E. A partner that wants USB3 together with DisplayPort takes it;
one that does not keeps pin assignment C. A dock that can do both and
prefers multi-function now gets two lanes next to USB3, so modes above
the bandwidth of two lanes, such as 3840x2160 at 60 Hz, are not offered
there. Pin assignment F is not offered.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: a monitor offering only pin assignment C still
gets it in both plug orientations; pin assignment D not tested, no sink
offering it was at hand.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index b217ceea5135..3927cb05e8d2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -552,11 +552,11 @@ connector {
 			/* USB default current, now stated as a PD source */
 			source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 900, PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM)>;
 
-			/* DisplayPort alternate mode, pin assignments C and E */
+			/* DisplayPort alternate mode, pin assignments C, D and E */
 			altmodes {
 				displayport {
 					svid = /bits/ 16 <0xff01>;
-					vdo = <0x00001446>;
+					vdo = <0x00001c46>;
 				};
 			};
 
